Another name for programmed I-O is [[Polling]]

**The problem with programmed I/O**

```C
while (!quit) {
	x = poll();
}
int poll() {
	while(!RDR_full) {
		read(); /*Lame ass busy wait*/
	}
	return value
}
```
As an alternative approach
```C
while (!quit) {
	x = poll();
}
int still_pretty_lame() {
	if(!RDR_full) {
		read(); /*Still checking every time*/
		return value
	}
	return dummy_value
}
```
This can still lead to an [[overrun]]
